{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "077K", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-gabber}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5add5b7d051afe3eb9a5804842cd2efd498161b0464498f4f83da0c3718dd646", "source_text": "Gabber's result", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9bc14ef3675a2e1afdde0cc1511fc909d9ac3a9bb8c1f07636cb2aa90ab9c728", "unit_id": "tag:077K:title"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "077K", "placeholders": {"FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001": "}", "FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001": "\\footnote{", "MATH_0001": "$\\kappa$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\kappa$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "TEXTCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTOPEN_0001": "\\href{https://amathew.wordpress.com/2011/07/30/quasi-coherent-sheaves-presentable-categories-and-a-result-of-gabber/}{"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:03e841948d1e66361eb5f4871a23ca2524cf7d78246f64325343258976ef65db", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6853cf7dd45f838a97e7ddcf7f6db730fc489223d7e738fcd9d6cf24339e469c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nIn this section we prove a result of Gabber which guarantees that on every\nscheme there exists a cardinal <MATH_0001> such that every quasi-coherent\nmodule <MATH_0002> is the union of its quasi-coherent\n<MATH_0003>-generated subsheaves. It follows that the category of quasi-coherent\nsheaves on a scheme is a Grothendieck abelian category having\nlimits and enough injectives<FOOTNOTEOPEN_0001>Nicely explained in a\n<TEXTOPEN_0001>blog post<TEXTCLOSE_0001>\nby Akhil Mathew.<FOOTNOTECLOSE_0001>.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9a235b31e841b37c93ca07e823a12c06faa533065803c075e217782fd9768c08", "unit_id": "tag:077K:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "077K", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(X, \\mathcal{O}_X)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\kappa$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\kappa$", "MATH_0006": "$X = \\bigcup U_i$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{F}|_{U_i}$", "MATH_0008": "$R_i \\subset \\mathcal{F}(U_i)$", "MATH_0009": "$\\kappa$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-kappa-generated}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dffd3332e8e4cec56a2048725644d00c270570dd6edf5258dd05c0caac46da1a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dd0ecdbf5ca062cca17d079ed6f2e6743b8c9602c7f4a3b45c1c71382bd25dc7", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ringed space. Let <MATH_0002> be an infinite\ncardinal. We say a sheaf of <MATH_0003>-modules <MATH_0004> is\n<TEXTITOPEN_0001><MATH_0005>-generated<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if there exists an open covering\n<MATH_0006> such that <MATH_0007> is generated by\na subset <MATH_0008> whose cardinality is\nat most <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bc2043faa58601a71a762e53bf408bbf3bbf49d4a4e7fa1b4b5d696b5fd746cb", "unit_id": "tag:077L:statement"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "077K", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\kappa$", "MATH_0002": "$\\kappa$", "MATH_0003": "$\\kappa$", "MATH_0004": "$\\kappa \\otimes \\kappa = \\kappa$", "MATH_0005": "$\\kappa$", "MATH_0006": "$\\kappa$", "MATH_0007": "$\\kappa$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{sets-section-cardinals}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:de1c56bbab04d8d951a6c2440cd9aee6048f0855d3328085cd3ba2277b51e833", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:50b71852aeecf1fe95cbee564935b41f44191d10329bc67bd62c7138ac18bda0", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNote that a direct sum of at most <MATH_0001> <MATH_0002>-generated modules is\nagain <MATH_0003>-generated because <MATH_0004>, see\nSets, Section <REF_0001>.\nIn particular this holds for the direct sum of two <MATH_0005>-generated modules.\nMoreover, a quotient of a <MATH_0006>-generated sheaf is <MATH_0007>-generated.\n(But the same needn't be true for submodules.)\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a514badebb3b13021a0605bfcb1506c72154d7e615e2149cbe0f0ef67c00317c", "unit_id": "tag:077K:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "077K", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$(X, \\mathcal{O}_X)$", "MATH_0002": "$\\kappa$", "MATH_0003": "$T$", "MATH_0004": "$(\\mathcal{F}_t)_{t \\in T}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\kappa$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0007": "$\\kappa$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0009": "$\\mathcal{F}_t$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-set-of-iso-classes}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:be975596608b76cc6d1f9d4b6caa4a6da36dcce4f12e17882c0307e69c0d12d5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:03d738958c2d515f29c9509bf2ec03b73d6bae5da456d1aa37a162ceb9c3639f", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a ringed space. Let <MATH_0002> be a cardinal.\nThere exists a set <MATH_0003> and a family <MATH_0004> of\n<MATH_0005>-generated <MATH_0006>-modules such that every <MATH_0007>-generated\n<MATH_0008>-module is isomorphic to one of the <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ae3dd4817e804106dd890383fe520ff2c123ad5955ac574957b0057f0b6ab547", "unit_id": "tag:077M:statement"}
